.el .ds Aq '
.TH "bead comment unresolve" 1  "bead comment unresolve " 
.SH NAME
bead comment unresolve \- Return a comment to unresolved
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbead comment unresolve\fR [\fB\-\-actor\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIISSUE_ID\fR> <\fICOMMENT_ID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Return one comment to unresolved.
.PP
The inverse of `comment resolve`, with the same selector rules and no\-op
safety: an already\-unresolved comment \- including an imported comment
whose stored resolution state is NULL \- is a no\-op that exits 0 and
emits no event. The comment\*(Aqs stored author is never changed.
.PP
EXAMPLES:
  bead comment unresolve bead\-123abc456789def comment\-1a2b3c4d
  bead comment unresolve bead\-123abc456789def comment\-1a2b3c4d \-\-actor reviewer \-\-json
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-actor\fR \fI<ACTOR>\fR
Attribution recorded in the audit event (defaults to BEAD_ACTOR, then system)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the JSON result envelope instead of the comment ID
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Validate and project the result without committing
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIISSUE_ID\fR>
Issue carrying the comment
.TP
<\fICOMMENT_ID\fR>
Comment to transition
